<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Dao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">276–339</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Dao was a Chinese statesman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-clan-of-langya">Wang clan of Langya</a> who guided the founding of the Eastern Jin dynasty. He advised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yuan-of-jin">Sima Rui</a> to move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jianye</a> in 307, won over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a> families of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>, and served as chief minister under the first three Eastern Jin emperors. His family's power was such that a saying ran 'the Wang and the Sima share the realm'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-dao.jpg" alt="Wang Dao" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 著者:顧沅（清） · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NAJDA-290-0047_%E5%8F%A4%E8%81%96%E8%B3%A2%E5%83%8F%E4%BC%9D%E7%95%A55_(%E7%8E%8B%E5%B0%8E).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
